                <note rend="inline" type="source">767.68119 P 43/1a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Child</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-28T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 28,
                                1922—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>161. The President desires you to be one of the observers to be present at
                    Lausanne during the peace conference. Mr. Grew, the American Minister at Berne,
                    will be associated with you in this work, and in addition, Admiral Bristol will
                    be requested to be present in Lausanne for such time as he can be appropriately
                    spared from his post at Constantinople. The Department is advising Mr. Grew and
                    Admiral Bristol accordingly. Department will take up with you and Mr. Grew later
                    the question of secretarial and clerical personnel.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
